@startuml
title Step 2 - Change configuration values and validate

actor person
participant "EngagementManagement" as EM
participant "ProductConfigurator" as PC

== POCV delegates to configurator the cart configuration responsability ==

activate EM
activate PC
note right of PC : still possible to do a **TMF760 Product Configuration** GET /queryProductConfiguration/1 if resource has been created
note right of PC : engagement is dealing directly with Product Configurator component

loop Till user configures offer
    person -> EM : 20 configure item
    EM -> PC : 21 **TMF760 Product Configuration** POST /queryProductConfiguration\n(ProductConfiguration.id1, selected offering + characteristic values)
    PC --> EM : 22 **TMF760** 200 OK\n(ProductConfiguration.id1, configuration updated with offerings, pricing,\ncharacteristics and actions possible)\nOR 201 Created (queryProductConfiguration.idX...)
    EM -> EM : 23 display new configuration\nand prices
end

person -> EM : 24 validate configuration
EM -> PC : 25 **TMF760 Product Configuration** POST /checkProductConfiguration\n(ProductConfiguration.id1 : latest configuration selected by user for\nmain selected offerings (items for fiber and add-ons))
PC --> EM : 26 **TMF760** 200 OK\n(state=approved)\nOR 201 Created
deactivate PC

note over EM, PC
  At this step, the main offerings have been configured, and the configuration is valid.
  The next offerings to be configured (shipping) are known by Engagement Management from latest POST queryProductConfiguration
end note
deactivate EM

@enduml
